      "source": "Bangsal Gusti Nurul",
      "description": "Bangsal Gusti Nurul or Pavilion Gusti Nurul, is the place where the king of Mangkunegara's family held a meeting together. Until now, the area included behind Pendhapa Ageng is often used for meetings and family photos.\nBangsal Gusti Nurul or Pavilion Gusti Nurul was designed by Mangkunegara IV in collaboration with Ir. Thomas Karsten as an architect graduated from Delft in the Netherlands, to repay the services of the princess Gusti Nurul. It has the flavor of the pavilion belonging to the Yogyakarta Pakualam Palace, but the Gusti Nurul Pavilion represents the taste of the Mangkunegara family.",
